\n\nDeliverable: `agents/literature/01a0a532-0b4d-7aa2-9ffb-b2b1c788bd86/lbv_followup/REPORT.md`\n\nFound 3 public CH4/air rows from Porowski et al. Energies 2024, Table 3:\n`S_U = 0.2348, 0.273335, 0.309474 m/s` at `298.15, 323.15, 348.15 K`, `1 bar`, stoichiometric.\n\nKey caveat: these are Bradley/Mitcheson model-derived from closed-vessel pressure traces, not direct canonical free-flame LBV measurements, and I did not find a formal uncertainty bound. I recommended low-weight validation only. Evidence archived as `evidence_d27619d4fd46f20457630782752cf874` and `evidence_7f9e0d7bbd59a04a021c7b5a08e628dd`.", "request_id": "72161079a3f2fcda7b7aeea72c14d356fabd6e5e848ecb4b1877693434c3c601", "status": "IDLE", "updated_at": 1789479313.0348456}}}
